---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="Privacy Policy for the Clockwork Otter Foundry website.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[var(--content-max-width)] px-6 py-24">
    <div class="max-w-[var(--reading-max-width)]">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Effective date: August 1, 2026</p>

      <p class="mt-6 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Clockwork Otter Foundry respects the privacy of visitors to this website. We have
        intentionally designed this site to collect as little personal information as reasonably
        possible.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">Information We Collect</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Clockwork Otter Foundry does not currently provide user accounts, login functionality,
        contact forms, analytics services, advertising trackers, or behavioral profiling on this
        website.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        We do not intentionally collect personal information from visitors simply for browsing the
        site.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        If you choose to contact us by email, we receive the information you voluntarily include
        in that communication, such as your email address, name if provided, message content, and
        any other information you choose to send.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">Email Communications</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        The email links on this website open your own email application or service. The website
        does not submit your message through a Clockwork Otter Foundry web form.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Information you send by email will be used to read, respond to, and manage your inquiry
        and for reasonable business recordkeeping related to that correspondence.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        We do not use email inquiries to enroll you in marketing communications without a separate
        appropriate basis for doing so.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">Cookies and Analytics</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Clockwork Otter Foundry does not currently use analytics services, advertising
        technologies, behavioral tracking, or tracking cookies on this website.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        The site should not introduce analytics, advertising, tracking, or other non-essential
        third-party technologies without first reviewing and updating this Privacy Policy and any
        consent requirements that may apply.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">Hosting and Technical Information</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        This website is hosted using GitHub Pages, a service provided by GitHub.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        GitHub may process routine technical information when visitors access the website in order
        to deliver, operate, maintain, and secure its services. GitHub states that visitor IP
        addresses for GitHub Pages sites are logged and stored for security purposes. GitHub's
        broader privacy practices may also cover service-usage information such as device,
        session, and request information.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        This processing is governed by GitHub's own privacy terms and practices.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Clockwork Otter Foundry does not use GitHub Pages visitor information for its own
        advertising or behavioral analytics.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">Third-Party Services and Links</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        This website may contain links to third-party websites or services. When you follow a
        third-party link, that service's own terms and privacy practices apply.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        GitHub Pages provides the website's hosting infrastructure.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Website fonts should be served locally by this website rather than loaded from Google
        Fonts or another external font CDN.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">How We Use Information</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        When you voluntarily provide personal information by contacting us, we use it only as
        reasonably necessary to:
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        <li>respond to your inquiry;</li>
        <li>communicate with you about the subject of your message;</li>
        <li>maintain appropriate business records;</li>
        <li>protect the security and integrity of our communications; and</li>
        <li>comply with applicable legal obligations.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">We do not sell personal information.</p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        We do not use information submitted through ordinary email correspondence for behavioral
        advertising.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">Legal Basis</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Where applicable data-protection law requires a legal basis for processing, the basis will
        depend on the context of the communication and may include responding to a request you
        initiated, taking steps at your request, complying with legal obligations, or legitimate
        interests in operating the business and responding to correspondence.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">Data Minimization and Retention</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        We intend to retain personal information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the
        purpose for which it was received, including responding to correspondence, maintaining
        appropriate business records, resolving disputes, protecting legal rights, and meeting
        applicable legal obligations.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Information that is no longer reasonably needed should be deleted or otherwise handled in
        accordance with applicable requirements.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">International Processing</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Because the website and services used to operate it may involve infrastructure located in
        different countries, technical information or communications may be processed outside the
        country in which a visitor resides.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Where applicable law imposes requirements on international transfers of personal
        information, those requirements should be addressed based on the services actually in use.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">Privacy Rights</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Depending on where you live and the law that applies, you may have rights relating to
        personal information about you, including rights to request access, correction, deletion,
        restriction, portability, or objection to certain processing.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        You may contact us at
        <a href="mailto:info@clockworkotterfoundry.com" class="font-medium">info@clockworkotterfoundry.com</a>
        with a privacy-related request.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Where applicable, individuals may also have the right to lodge a complaint with the
        relevant data-protection authority.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        This website is a general informational website and is not directed specifically to
        children.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Clockwork Otter Foundry does not knowingly use this website to solicit personal
        information from children.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">Security</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        We take reasonable steps appropriate to the nature of this website and the limited
        information we receive to protect information under our control. However, no internet
        transmission, email system, or storage system can be guaranteed to be completely secure.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        We may update this Privacy Policy if the website, our practices, the services we use, or
        applicable requirements change.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        When the policy is updated, the effective date shown at the top of the page should also be
        updated.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Material additions such as analytics, forms, accounts, tracking, advertising, payment
        processing, or new third-party data-processing services must trigger a privacy review
        before deployment.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">Contact</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        For questions about this Privacy Policy or privacy-related requests:
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 font-semibold text-[var(--color-text-primary)]">Clockwork Otter Foundry</p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        <strong>Email:</strong>
        <a href="mailto:info@clockworkotterfoundry.com" class="font-medium">info@clockworkotterfoundry.com</a>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        <strong>Business/legal identity and mailing address:</strong>
        [TODO: business legal identity and mailing address to be finalized]
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
